---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import murrayGreyImage from "../assets/images/4.webp";
---

<section class="bg-cream-dark py-16 lg:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-12 px-6 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-20">
        <Image
            src={murrayGreyImage}
            alt="One of the Ferguson Livestock Murray Grey cattle"
            class="aspect-square w-full object-cover"
            widths={[500, 720, 960]}
            sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 50vw"
        />

        <div>
            <p class="mb-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-sage">Why Murray Grey</p>
            <h2 class="mb-6 font-display text-4xl font-semibold leading-none text-forest sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">The breed at the centre of our farm.</h2>
            <div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700">
                <p>Murray Greys are part of Victoria’s cattle story, and they are the breed we have chosen to build Ferguson Livestock around.</p>
                <p>We value cattle that are calm to work with, suited to our farm and capable of producing a balanced eating experience. Showing the herd keeps us focused on the details—structure, temperament, preparation and consistency.</p>
                <p>Our cattle achievements are proof of the breeding work behind Ferguson Livestock. We keep those claims separate from the beef itself: good marketing should be as traceable as the product.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="/our-story" class="mt-8 inline-block border-b-2 border-sage pb-1 font-semibold text-forest no-underline hover:text-sage">Why we chose the breed →</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
